archives-baccarat-catalogue-cartes-posta.description:
A set of old documents from the Compagnie des Cristalleries de Baccarat, probably gathered by a dealer or a representative of the firm. A little archive for collectors of Baccarat crystal, tableware and company papers.

The lot includes:
· a catalogue “Baccarat, Galeries d’exposition, 30 bis rue de Paradis, Paris 10e”, leather-look cover with gilt signature, with the famous page “Baccarat chez les chefs d’État” (glasses engraved with the arms of the King of Egypt, the King of Spain, the King of Italy, King Charles X, the Presidency of the French Republic, the United States Embassy…) and the firm’s coat of arms;
· old unwritten postcards: the Cristalleries de Baccarat stand at the 1909 Nancy Exhibition (2 views), the Baccarat and Christofle pavilion at the 1925 Decorative Arts Exhibition, the small showroom of the Paris sales shops, and the general view of the Baccarat works;
· a printed business card of a representative of the Compagnie des Cristalleries de Baccarat (1900s);
· two workshop photographic prints of engraved glass and decanter models, with model numbers (14739, 8445) and prices noted on the back;
· a plate no. 47 at 1/4 scale, a typed price sheet, a “service Zurich” leaflet;
· an invoice on Compagnie des Cristalleries de Baccarat letterhead dated 31 December 1958, for Châteaubriant and Marengo glasses (the customer’s name is blurred in the photos).

Condition: period documents, yellowed paper, folds, small tears and pencil notes; catalogue cover rubbed, with a missing piece at the bottom left. Everything shows in the real photos. Sold as a single set.

cd-tesoros-musica-espana-estampas-de-esp.description:
Spain through the eyes of the great composers, in 11 tracks:
· Chabrier, España, rhapsody for orchestra;
· Debussy, Ibéria (Par les rues et par les chemins, Les parfums de la nuit, Le matin d’un jour de fête);
· Bizet, Carmen, suites no. 1 and 2 (Aragonaise, Séguedille, Les Toréadors, Habanera, the Toreador Song);
· Tchaikovsky, the Spanish Dance from Swan Lake;
· Rimsky-Korsakov, Capriccio espagnol.
Performed by the London Festival Orchestra (Alfred Scholz), the ORF Symphony Orchestra (Milan Horvat) and the Philharmonia Slavonica (Alberto Lizzio).

Audio CD, number 2 in the Spanish collection “Tesoros de la Música de España”, published by Espasa with the newspaper ABC in 2000, presented in a DVD-size case.

Condition: case, sleeve and disc in good condition. CD not tested. The real photos show everything.

chaine-medailles-religieuses-anciennes-l.description:
Seven pilgrimage and devotional keepsakes from the early 20th century, kept together the way families used to:
· a quatrefoil medal: the veiled Virgin in profile, with “Souvenir du Calvaire” on the reverse;
· a rectangular “Virgo Carmeli” medal (Our Lady of Mount Carmel), with the Sacred Heart on the reverse;
· a scalloped “Sainte Anne d’Auray, priez pour nous” medal, with “Sainte Anne, patronne de la Bretagne, protégez-nous” on the reverse;
· a star-shaped cross, “N.-D. de Lourdes, priez pour nous”;
· an openwork oval medal of the Virgin;
· a small crucifix, “Souvenir de N.-D. de Lourdes”;
· a large I.N.R.I. crucifix, “Souvenir de mission”.
White metal and aluminium medals, with a lovely patina of use and no visible breakage. They are gathered on a simple metal chain that is only there to hold them: the value is in the medals. Keep them together, hang them up or take them off for a creation of your own. Real photos, fronts and backs.

lot-13-cartes-mignonnettes-bonne-annee-1.description:
Thirteen “mignonnettes”, those little greeting cards that were slipped into an envelope with a few words on the back, as families did at the end of every year. Twelve “Bonne Année” (Happy New Year) and one “Anniversaire” (Birthday):
· little girls and boys with their puppies, a little girl in a pansy dress, children under a daisy;
· baskets of daisies, garlands of flowers, roses and holly, pansies;
· two cards decorated with a real tied silk ribbon and painted flowers, one embossed silver card, one gold embossed card.

On the back, wishes written in ink between 31 December 1927 and 29 December 1932, by a sister, a goddaughter or a niece to “cher frère”, “cher parrain et marraine”, with all the tenderness and spelling of the time. A small piece of family history from between the wars.

Size approx. 11 x 6 cm. Condition: yellowed paper, corners and edges slightly rubbed, original ribbons. Everything shows in the real photos. Sent flat, by letter post.

lot-3-classiques-pour-tous-hatier-eschyl.description:
Three booklets from the famous little school collection “Les Classiques pour tous” by Librairie A. Hatier (8, rue d’Assas, Paris), with their pretty covers featuring a frieze and medallion:
· Aeschylus, Les Perses, no. 447, translation;
· Virgil, Bucoliques, Géorgiques, no. 157, translation (printed by Brodard et Taupin, legal deposit 1953);
· Gustave Flaubert, Salammbô, volume I, no. 569 (printed in Alençon in 1948), with the stamp of a school, the Institution Notre-Dame de Pontmain (Mayenne).

Schoolbooks of yesteryear, for lovers of ancient literature, old paper or bookshelf decor. Please note: only volume I of Salammbô is included.

Condition: period paperbacks, yellowed paper, covers slightly rubbed and stained, a few pencil notes. Each booklet complete. Everything shows in the real photos.

lot-5-cartes-de-voeux-anciennes-1928-193.description:
Five pretty greeting cards from days gone by:
· a folded “Meilleurs Vœux” (Best Wishes) card with a satin fabric flower in a medallion, laid paper and a pink silk cord, with a little blue note inside written to a niece;
· a “Bonne Année” with a bell tower in the snow at sunset;
· a painted card with a bluebird in its nest in the snow, in front of a chapel;
· a “Bonne Année” with pink cyclamens;
· an EKO no. 557 card with pansies, embossed gold lettering and a cut-out landscape.

On the back, handwritten end-of-year wishes, including cards dated 30 December 1928 and 30 December 1930, addressed to “cher frère et sœur” and to the nieces.

Condition: yellowed paper, a few stains and rubbed corners. Everything shows in the real photos. Sent flat, by letter post.

vhs-albator-ii-canestrier-junior-collect.description:
An Albator VHS published by Jacques Canestrier, the man who introduced French children to Goldorak and Albator: a 1980s edition sought after by anime collectors and anyone nostalgic for Récré A2.

A “Spécial 4 épisodes” of Leiji Matsumoto’s cult series (Toei Animation, 1978), in the original French dub, with music by Éric Charden, Didier Barbelivien and Guy Matteoni:
· L’Armada royale;
· Les Humanoïdes végétales;
· Le Traquenard de la reine;
· La Planète des fleurs sauvages.
The Arcadia against the Sylvidres and their queen Sylvidra, with Albator, Clio and Alfred.

Colour SECAM VHS, French version, about 1 h 30, “Junior Collection”, Jacques Canestrier Vidéo, in its large white case with its original sleeve.

Condition: sleeve in good used condition with some rubbing and a slight crease on the back, case slightly yellowed. Tape not tested. You’ll need a VCR to play it. Everything shows in the real photos.
